# {packageName} client library for .NET

{packageName} simplifies declarative resource provisioning in .NET.

## Getting started

### Install the package

Install the provisioning library for .NET with [NuGet](https://www.nuget.org/):

```dotnetcli
dotnet add package {packageName} --prerelease
```

### Prerequisites

You must have an [Azure subscription](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/dotnet/).

## Key concepts

Define your infrastructure in C# using `Infrastructure`, `ProvisionableResource`,
and `BicepValue<T>`. Build the infrastructure into Bicep templates and deploy
them with Azure Developer CLI (`azd`) or your preferred Azure deployment tools.

## Examples

See the [Azure.Provisioning examples][provisioning] for defining resources,
parameters, and outputs.

